CORE
main.c
--unwind 2 --rounds 2 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Racy control for `store_through_pointer_framing`: main locks `mB` when it
writes `dA`, while the thread writes `dA` under `mA`. The race is on the
store itself, not on any framing read, so it must stay FAILED before and
after the fix.
